From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:19:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(telemetry): record the model and effort a turn ran with

The agent span only carried what a turn asked for. With no model pinned,
gen_ai.request.model and llm.model_name fell back to the agent name, and
no effort was recorded at all, so a session on the defaults never said
which model or effort ran.

gen_ai.request.model is now set only when the turn requested a model.
The agent name stays in gen_ai.agent.name, and llm.model_name and
gen_ai.provider.name are unchanged for MLflow and OpenInference views.
The agent span also gets:

- gen_ai.response.model with omnigent.model.source: observed from the
  turn's usage model (SDK harnesses), or requested when only the turn's
  override is known. An observed value replaces the requested one at
  turn end.
- omnigent.reasoning_effort.requested (as given), and
  omnigent.reasoning_effort with .source, only when the level is known:
  requested, or observed when the harness reports what it applied.
  Codex now reports its thread default on TurnComplete; harnesses that
  report nothing (Claude Code, Claude Agent SDK, pi, OpenAI Agents) leave
  a default effort unset.

Nothing changes when telemetry is off.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
